e draw a dashed line.\n- Then, we must decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality $y \\lt -2x + 20$ refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* those on the line $y = -2x + 20$. So, we shade *below* the line.\n- Lastly, because $x$ and $y$ cannot be negative, we limit our shading to the first quadrant.\n\n![](images/3c/3c2c2af356747fbf9d1e2a9d03fe98ed211e36af11032930682d6d08ca0bfa5c.png)" 13194139539081 17592186576411 true] [17592186105518 1074 "The total cost of renting is $70x + 35y$. Since the event planner's budget is less than $700$, we have the following inequality:\n$70x + 35y \\mid < 700$\n\nTo plot this inequality, we will first convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}70x + 35y & < 700 \\\\ 2x + y & < 20 \\\\ y & < - 2x + 20\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nLet's now draw the region.\n\n- Since the inequality involves a 'less than' sign, the line $y = -2x + 20$ is not part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a dashed line.\n- Then, we must decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality $y \\lt -2x + 20$ refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* those on the line $y = -2x + 20$. So, we shade *below* the line.\n- Lastly, because $x$ and $y$ cannot be negative, we limit our shading to the first quadrant.\n\n![](images/3c/3c2c2af356747fbf9d1e2a9d03fe98ed211e36af11032930682d6d08ca0bfa5c.png)" 13194139539081 17592186576411 false] [17592186105519 1074 "Let's answer the questions in turn.\n\n- To determine whether the artist can fulfill the order, we need to test if the point $(4,3)$ belongs to the feasible region. The graph shows that $(4,3)$ belongs to the region. Therefore, the artist can fulfill the order.\n\n![](images/3b/3b766502f87488894b2ec94f582d5ad6b123baea701627bd3760daa23a6e13a2.png)\n\n- Selling $x=4$ sculptures and $y=3$ paintings, the artist obtains a revenue of\n$$\n\\displaystyle 1600x + 1200y|= \\[math]1600 \\cdot 4 + \\[/math]1200 \\cdot 3; = \\[math]6400 + \\[/math]3600; = \\[math]10000.\n